@*
    The block a domain surface mounts when it wants integrations at all.

    Thin on purpose. It owns the order of the four parts and one precedence rule,
    and nothing else — it is not a container, and the moment it starts deciding
    what goes inside it, four surfaces will be passing it four sets of options to
    get four layouts back.

    It earns its place anyway, because without it every surface composes the same
    three parts in its own order and half the consistency this family exists for
    goes unmet: a reader would learn where the acts are on a backlog entry and
    have to learn it again on a knowledge chapter.

    The order is fixed: header and freshness, then the acts, then the references,
    then whatever the surface adds. Acts before references because an act is what
    a reader came to do and a reference is what already happened.

    The one precedence rule: when the whole cluster is unavailable the acts are
    replaced by the reason, and the references stay. A pull request read last
    Tuesday is still open today; blanking it because a token expired would tell
    the reader something false, and quietly is the worst way to be wrong.
*@

<section class="@ClassValue" data-testid="@TestId">
    <header class="integration-panel__header" data-testid="@HeaderTestId">
        <h3 class="integration-panel__title">@Title</h3>

        <IntegrationFreshness Reading="@Reading" Density="@Density" OnRefresh="@OnRefresh" />
    </header>

    @if (Cluster.IsAvailable)
    {
        <div class="integration-panel__actions" data-testid="@ActionsTestId">
            <IntegrationActionBar Actions="@Actions"
                                  Density="@Density"
                                  AriaLabel="@Title"
                                  OnInvoke="@OnInvoke"
                                  OnCancel="@OnCancel"
                                  OnRetry="@OnRetry"
                                  OnRemedy="@OnRemedy" />
        </div>
    }
    else
    {
        <IntegrationUnavailable Readiness="@Cluster" Density="@Density" OnRemedy="@OnRemedy" />
    }

    <div class="integration-panel__links" data-testid="@LinksTestId">
        @* No Reading and no OnRefresh: the header already carries the one
           freshness line this panel has, and a second one inside the list would
           be the same fact stated twice a few pixels apart. And no Readiness
           either — the reason is stated once above, and repeating it over the
           references is what would make them look untrustworthy. *@
        <IntegrationLinkList Links="@Links"
                             Density="@Density"
                             OnOpen="@OnOpen" />
    </div>

    @ChildContent
</section>

@code {
    [Parameter]
    public string Title { get; set; } = "Integrations";

    [Parameter]
    public IReadOnlyList<IntegrationActionSpec> Actions { get; set; } = [];

    [Parameter]
    public IReadOnlyList<IntegrationLinkRef> Links { get; set; } = [];

    [Parameter]
    public IntegrationReading Reading { get; set; } = IntegrationReading.Never;

    [Parameter]
    public IntegrationReadiness? Readiness { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public IntegrationDensity Density { get; set; } = IntegrationDensity.Toolbar;

    /// <summary>Anything the surface adds under the standard parts — open
    /// proposals, an extra row. Last, because it is the part this panel knows
    /// nothing about and cannot order against.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<IntegrationActionSpec> OnInvoke { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<IntegrationActionSpec> OnCancel { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<IntegrationActionSpec> OnRetry { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<IntegrationReadiness> OnRemedy { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<IntegrationLinkRef> OnOpen { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback OnRefresh { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string? CssClass { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string? TestId { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string? HeaderTestId { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string? ActionsTestId { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string? LinksTestId { get; set; }

    private IntegrationReadiness Cluster => Readiness ?? IntegrationReadiness.Ready;

    private string ClassValue
    {
        get
        {
            var stem = $"integration-panel integration-panel--{IntegrationStates.SlugOf(Density)}";
            return string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(CssClass) ? stem : $"{stem} {CssClass}";
        }
    }
}
